Track 2: Opal, Did the Larva Hatch in Bay 4?
- Story & Context: Squatting in the dead LensCrafters across from the shuttered pretzel stall, Opal Chen used their canine teeth to strip enamel off copper wire, tasting bitter grease while their homebrew vocoder tracked through a hacked Galaga audio daughterboard. Ren had vanished down the service tunnels two nights earlier following a screaming match over cracked vacuum tubes, leaving behind only his scarred fluegelhorn and three hundred dead capacitors ticking in the winter draft. Crying silently into the throat-mic until the ribbon element distorted against the monitor’s 15kHz hum, Opal harmonized with the vacant store’s acoustic bounce to utter, "you traded your wings for another free credit." The take was captured in a single unedited pass, standing as the scene’s most devastating confession of abandonment and grief.
