Track 3: Tilt-Lock Metamorphosis
- Story & Context: Years after the bulldozers crushed the Galleria into concrete dust, urban explorers unearthed a lead-sealed flight case wedged inside the air duct of the old food court mezzanine. Inside, a weather-beaten quarter-inch tape survived, containing the final mythic jam recorded the night the power grid permanently failed and a cloud of pale lunar moths swarmed through the shattered skylights into the stage lights. As the band played through dying automotive batteries, the horn lines dissolved into impossible, microtonal vocoder cascades that imitated the flutter of insect wings, offering one final choral whisper: "we are shedding our plastic skins beneath the rubble." The tape abruptly terminates with the thud of an arcade tilt-sensor engaging, sealing the legend of the mall's ghost choir forever.
